/-!
# Equidistribution of subset sums of random subsets of abelian groups (Erdős Problem 1179)

This file proves `balancedSubsetSumsThresholdLogTwo_holds`: for every `0 < ε < 1`, a uniformly
random subset of size `(1 + o(1)) log₂ N` of a finite abelian group of order `N` is `ε`-balanced
with probability tending to `1` as `N → ∞`, and every `ε`-balanced subset `A` of a group of order
`N` satisfies `N ≤ 2 ^ |A|`.

Erdős Problem 1179: for `0 < ε < 1` let `g_ε(N)` be the least `k` such that for an abelian group `G`
of size `N` and a uniformly random `k`-subset `A`, with probability `→ 1` as `N → ∞` every `g ∈ G`
has `|F_A(g) - 2^k/N| ≤ ε 2^k/N`, where `F_A(g)` counts subsets of `A` with sum `g`. Is `g_ε(N) = (1
+ o_ε(1)) log₂ N`?

Source: T. F. Bloom, Erdős Problems, Problem #1179, https://www.erdosproblems.com/1179 (status
PROVED). UnsolvedMath record UM-30007220 (`EP-1179`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

The target states `g_ε(N) = (1 + o(1)) log₂ N` as two bounds. Upper: sizes `k(N) = (1 + o(1)) log₂
N` for which the success probability tends to `1` along every sequence of finite abelian groups with
`|G| → ∞` (equivalently, uniformly over the groups of order `N`). Lower: every `ε`-balanced subset
`A` of a group of order `N` has `2^{|A|} ≥ N`, so no size below `log₂ N` succeeds (the source calls
this bound trivial: balance with `ε < 1` makes every `g` a subset sum). Compared with the
formal-conjectures statement `ErdosProblems/1179.lean` (the conjunction of `erdos_1179` and
`erdos_1179.variants.lower_bound`; no code imported).

## Proof outline

The proof is a self-contained counting argument; write `N = |G|`.

* Tuples instead of subsets. For a tuple `f : ι → G`, count the subsets of `ι` whose entries sum to
  `g`. For an injective tuple this is `subsetSumCount` of its image, and every `k`-subset is the
  image of `k!` injective tuples, so when `2 k ^ 2 ≤ N` the probability that a uniformly random
  `k`-subset is not balanced is at most `2 / N ^ k` times the number of unbalanced tuples.
* Second moment. For two distinct subsets `s ≠ t` of `ι`, the difference of the sums over `s` and
  `t` is a surjective homomorphism of the tuple, so
  `∑ f, ∑ g, (count - 2 ^ k / N) ^ 2 ≤ 2 ^ k N ^ k`.
* High moments of hitting counts. For `B ⊆ G`, the number `H(c)` of subsets of the index set of
  `c : ι → G` (with `|ι| = m`) whose sum lies in `B` satisfies
  `∑ c, H(c) ^ p ≤ 2 ^ (2 ^ p) N ^ m max(1, 2 ^ m |B| / N) ^ p`. Expanding the `p`-th power
  gives `p`-tuples of subsets of `ι`, encoded by the rows `{i | j ∈ U i} ∈ {0,1}^p`, `j ∈ ι`. If
  the subgroup of `ℤ^p` generated by the set `T` of rows projects onto the coordinates `I`, the
  sums over `U i`, `i ∈ I`, form a surjective homomorphism `G^ι → G^I`, so at most
  `N ^ m (|B| / N) ^ |I|` tuples `c` hit `B` at every coordinate. A lattice lemma provides such
  an `I` with `|T| ≤ 2 ^ |I|`: a coset of a subgroup of `ℤ^p` contains at most `2 ^ |I|` points
  of `{0,1}^p` for some coordinates `I` onto which the subgroup projects (induction on the
  coordinates).
* Two stages. Split the tuple into blocks of sizes `k₁ = log₂ N + o(log N)` and `m = o(log N)`.
  By the second moment and the hitting-count bound for singletons, for most first blocks the
  counts are within `ε / 2` of their mean outside a small set `B` and at most `K` times their mean
  everywhere. The counts of the whole tuple average those of the first block over the `2 ^ m`
  subset sums of the second block, so they stay balanced unless some translate of `B` is hit too
  often, which the hitting-count bound makes rare.
* Parameters. With the moment order `p ≈ log₂ log₂ N`, the failure probability is at most
  `6 / 2 ^ p`, and the chosen size `k(N)` satisfies `k(N) / log₂ N → 1`.

The lower bound holds because an `ε`-balanced set with `ε < 1` has every element of `G` as a
subset sum, so `|G| ≤ 2 ^ |A|`.

## Implementation notes

The definitions and the statement keep the full names they had in the former wanted module, so
their namespace still ends in `Wanted`. All auxiliary declarations are private.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.Combinatorics.RandomSubsetSumsBalancedErdosProblem1179Wanted

open Filter Finset

open scoped Classical in
/-- **Number of subsets with a given sum.** For a finite subset $A$ of an abelian group $G$ and an
element $g \in G$, $F_A(g)$ is the number of subsets $S \subseteq A$, the empty set included, whose
elements sum to $g$, that is, with $\sum_{x \in S} x = g$. -/
noncomputable def subsetSumCount {G : Type*} [AddCommGroup G] (A : Finset G) (g : G) : ℕ :=
  (A.powerset.filter fun S => ∑ x ∈ S, x = g).card

/-- **$\varepsilon$-balanced subsets of a finite abelian group.** Let $G$ be a finite abelian group
with $N = |G|$ elements and let $\varepsilon$ be a real number. A subset $A \subseteq G$ is
$\varepsilon$-balanced when, for every $g \in G$, the number $F_A(g)$ of subsets of $A$ whose
elements sum to $g$ satisfies
$\left| F_A(g) - 2^{|A|}/N \right| \le \varepsilon \cdot 2^{|A|}/N$. -/
def IsBalanced {G : Type*} [AddCommGroup G] [Fintype G] (ε : ℝ) (A : Finset G) : Prop :=
  ∀ g : G, |(subsetSumCount A g : ℝ) - 2 ^ A.card / Fintype.card G| ≤
    ε * (2 ^ A.card / Fintype.card G)

open scoped Classical in
/-- **Probability that a random subset is balanced.** For a finite abelian group $G$, a real
number $\varepsilon$ and a natural number $k$, this is the number of $\varepsilon$-balanced
$k$-element subsets of $G$ divided by the number of all $k$-element subsets of $G$, that is, the
probability that a uniformly random $k$-element subset of $G$ is $\varepsilon$-balanced. When
$k > |G|$ there are no $k$-element subsets and the value is $0$. -/
noncomputable def balancedProbability (G : Type*) [AddCommGroup G] [Fintype G] (ε : ℝ) (k : ℕ) :
    ℝ :=
  (((univ : Finset G).powersetCard k).filter (IsBalanced ε)).card /
    ((univ : Finset G).powersetCard k).card

/-- **Erdős Problem 1179 (balanced subset sums of random subsets).** The statement of Erdős
Problem 1179 is the proposition that, for every real $\varepsilon$ with $0 < \varepsilon < 1$, the
following two bounds hold. Upper bound: there is a function $k : \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{N}$ with
$k(N) / \log_2 N \to 1$ as $N \to \infty$ such that, for every sequence $(G_i)_{i \in \mathbb{N}}$
of finite abelian groups with $|G_i| \to \infty$, the probability that a uniformly random
$k(|G_i|)$-element subset of $G_i$ is $\varepsilon$-balanced tends to $1$ as $i \to \infty$. Lower
bound: for every finite abelian group $G$, every $\varepsilon$-balanced subset $A \subseteq G$
satisfies $|G| \le 2^{|A|}$. -/
def balancedSubsetSumsThresholdLogTwo : Prop :=
  ∀ ε : ℝ, 0 < ε → ε < 1 →
    (∃ k : ℕ → ℕ, Tendsto (fun N : ℕ => (k N : ℝ) / Real.logb 2 N) atTop (nhds 1) ∧
      ∀ (G : ℕ → Type) [∀ i, AddCommGroup (G i)] [∀ i, Fintype (G i)],
        Tendsto (fun i => Fintype.card (G i)) atTop atTop →
          Tendsto (fun i => balancedProbability (G i) ε (k (Fintype.card (G i)))) atTop (nhds 1)) ∧
    ∀ (G : Type) [AddCommGroup G] [Fintype G] (A : Finset G), IsBalanced ε A →
      Fintype.card G ≤ 2 ^ A.card

/-! ### A lattice lemma -/

/-- Indicator vector in `ℤ^α` of a finite set of coordinates. -/
private def ind {α : Type*} [DecidableEq α] (s : Finset α) : α → ℤ :=
  fun i => if i ∈ s then 1 else 0

/-- `L` projects onto the coordinates `I`. -/
private def Spans {α : Type*} (L : AddSubgroup (α → ℤ)) (I : Finset α) : Prop :=
  ∀ z : α → ℤ, ∃ y ∈ L, ∀ i ∈ I, y i = z i

private lemma Spans.mono {α : Type*} {L L' : AddSubgroup (α → ℤ)} {I : Finset α} (h : Spans L I)
    (hL : L ≤ L') : Spans L' I := fun z => by
  obtain ⟨y, hy, hyz⟩ := h z
  exact ⟨y, hL hy, hyz⟩

private lemma spans_empty {α : Type*} (L : AddSubgroup (α → ℤ)) : Spans L ∅ :=
  fun _ => ⟨0, L.zero_mem, by simp⟩

private lemma ind_insert {α : Type*} [DecidableEq α] {a : α} {x : Finset α} (ha : a ∉ x) :
    ind (insert a x) = ind x + ind {a} := by
  funext i
  by_cases h : i = a
  · subst h; simp [ind, ha]
  · simp [ind, h]

open scoped Classical in
/-- A coset of a subgroup `L ≤ ℤ^α` contains at most `2 ^ |I|` vectors of `{0,1}^S`, for some
set `I` of coordinates onto which `L` projects. -/
private lemma lattice_count {α : Type*} [DecidableEq α] (S : Finset α) :
    ∀ (L : AddSubgroup (α → ℤ)) (v : α → ℤ), ∃ I : Finset α, Spans L I ∧
      #{x ∈ S.powerset | ind x - v ∈ L} ≤ 2 ^ #I := by
  induction S using Finset.induction_on with
  | empty =>
    intro L v
    refine ⟨∅, spans_empty L, ?_⟩
    simp only [card_empty, pow_zero]
    exact (card_filter_le _ _).trans (by simp)
  | insert a S ha ih =>
    intro L v
    set L0 : AddSubgroup (α → ℤ) := L ⊓ (Pi.evalAddMonoidHom (fun _ : α => ℤ) a).ker with hL0
    have mem_L0 : ∀ y, y ∈ L0 ↔ y ∈ L ∧ y a = 0 := fun y => by
      simp [hL0, AddSubgroup.mem_inf, AddMonoidHom.mem_ker]
    have hL0L : L0 ≤ L := inf_le_left
    have ind_a : ∀ x ∈ S.powerset, ind x a = 0 := fun x hx => by
      have : a ∉ x := fun h => ha (mem_powerset.1 hx h)
      simp [ind, this]
    -- split according to whether `a` belongs to the subset
    have hsplit : #{x ∈ (insert a S).powerset | ind x - v ∈ L} ≤
        #{x ∈ S.powerset | ind x - v ∈ L} + #{x ∈ S.powerset | ind (insert a x) - v ∈ L} := by
      rw [powerset_insert, filter_union, filter_image]
      exact (card_union_le _ _).trans (Nat.add_le_add_left card_image_le _)
    -- each part lies in a coset of `L0`
    have part : ∀ w : Finset α → α → ℤ, (∀ x ∈ S.powerset, w x = ind x + w ∅) →
        ∃ I : Finset α, Spans L0 I ∧ #{x ∈ S.powerset | w x - v ∈ L} ≤ 2 ^ #I := by
      intro w hw
      by_cases hne : ({x ∈ S.powerset | w x - v ∈ L} : Finset _).Nonempty
      · obtain ⟨x0, hx0⟩ := hne
        rw [mem_filter] at hx0
        obtain ⟨I, hI, hcard⟩ := ih L0 (ind x0)
        refine ⟨I, hI, le_trans (card_le_card ?_) hcard⟩
        intro x hx
        rw [mem_filter] at hx ⊢
        refine ⟨hx.1, (mem_L0 _).2 ⟨?_, ?_⟩⟩
        · have := L.sub_mem hx.2 hx0.2
          rw [hw x hx.1, hw x0 hx0.1] at this
          convert this using 1
          abel
        · simp [ind_a x hx.1, ind_a x0 hx0.1]
      · rw [not_nonempty_iff_eq_empty] at hne
        exact ⟨∅, spans_empty L0, by simp [hne]⟩
    obtain ⟨I0, hI0, hc0⟩ := part ind (fun x _ => by funext i; simp [ind])
    obtain ⟨I1, hI1, hc1⟩ := part (fun x => ind (insert a x))
      (fun x hx => by
        have : a ∉ x := fun h => ha (mem_powerset.1 hx h)
        rw [ind_insert this, ind_insert (notMem_empty a)]
        funext i; simp [ind])
    by_cases h0 : ({x ∈ S.powerset | ind x - v ∈ L} : Finset _).Nonempty
    · by_cases h1 : ({x ∈ S.powerset | ind (insert a x) - v ∈ L} : Finset _).Nonempty
      · obtain ⟨x0, hx0⟩ := h0
        obtain ⟨x1, hx1⟩ := h1
        rw [mem_filter] at hx0 hx1
        set w := ind (insert a x1) - ind x0 with hw
        have hwL : w ∈ L := by
          have := L.sub_mem hx1.2 hx0.2
          convert this using 1
          rw [hw]; abel
        have hwa : w a = 1 := by
          have : a ∉ x0 := fun h => ha (mem_powerset.1 hx0.1 h)
          simp [hw, ind, this]
        set J := if #I0 ≤ #I1 then I1 else I0 with hJ
        have hJs : Spans L0 J := by rw [hJ]; split_ifs <;> assumption
        have hc0' : #{x ∈ S.powerset | ind x - v ∈ L} ≤ 2 ^ #J := by
          refine hc0.trans (Nat.pow_le_pow_right (by norm_num) ?_)
          rw [hJ]; split_ifs with h <;> omega
        have hc1' : #{x ∈ S.powerset | ind (insert a x) - v ∈ L} ≤ 2 ^ #J := by
          refine hc1.trans (Nat.pow_le_pow_right (by norm_num) ?_)
          rw [hJ]; split_ifs with h <;> omega
        have haJ : a ∉ J := by
          intro haJ
          obtain ⟨y, hy, hyz⟩ := hJs (fun _ => 1)
          have := hyz a haJ
          rw [((mem_L0 y).1 hy).2] at this
          exact absurd this (by norm_num)
        refine ⟨insert a J, ?_, ?_⟩
        · intro z
          obtain ⟨y, hy, hyz⟩ := hJs (z - z a • w)
          refine ⟨y + z a • w, L.add_mem ((mem_L0 y).1 hy).1 (L.zsmul_mem hwL _), ?_⟩
          intro i hi
          rcases mem_insert.1 hi with rfl | hi
          · simp [((mem_L0 y).1 hy).2, hwa]
          · simp [hyz i hi]
        · rw [card_insert_of_notMem haJ, pow_succ]
          omega
      · rw [not_nonempty_iff_eq_empty] at h1
        refine ⟨I0, hI0.mono hL0L, hsplit.trans ?_⟩
        rw [h1, card_empty, add_zero]; exact hc0
    · rw [not_nonempty_iff_eq_empty] at h0
      refine ⟨I1, hI1.mono hL0L, hsplit.trans ?_⟩
      rw [h0, card_empty, zero_add]; exact hc1

/-! ### High moments of hitting counts -/

/-- Fibres of a surjective homomorphism of finite groups. -/
private lemma card_fiber_mul_card {A H : Type*} [AddGroup A] [Fintype A] [AddGroup H] [Fintype H]
    [DecidableEq H] (φ : A →+ H) (hφ : Function.Surjective φ) (x : H) :
    #{a | φ a = x} * Fintype.card H = Fintype.card A := by
  have h1 : Fintype.card A = ∑ y : H, #{a | φ a = y} := by
    rw [← Finset.card_univ]; exact card_eq_sum_card_fiberwise (fun _ _ => mem_univ _)
  have h2 : ∀ y, #{a | φ a = y} = #{a | φ a = x} := fun y =>
    AddMonoidHom.card_fiber_eq_of_mem_range φ (hφ y) (hφ x)
  rw [h1, Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun y _ => h2 y), sum_const, card_univ, smul_eq_mul, mul_comm]

variable {G : Type*} [AddCommGroup G] [Fintype G] [DecidableEq G]
variable {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι]

/-- The coordinates `i` whose subset `U i` contains `j`. -/
private def rowSet {p : ℕ} (U : Fin p → Finset ι) (j : ι) : Finset (Fin p) := {i | j ∈ U i}

omit [Fintype G] [DecidableEq G] [Fintype ι] in
private lemma exists_sum_eq_smul {p : ℕ} (U : Fin p → Finset ι) {y : Fin p → ℤ}
    (hy : y ∈ AddSubgroup.closure (Set.range fun j => ind (rowSet U j))) (g : G) :
    ∃ c : ι → G, ∀ i, ∑ j ∈ U i, c j = y i • g := by
  induction hy using AddSubgroup.closure_induction with
  | mem x hx =>
    obtain ⟨j, rfl⟩ := hx
    refine ⟨Pi.single j g, fun i => ?_⟩
    rw [Finset.sum_pi_single']
    simp [ind, rowSet]
  | zero => exact ⟨0, fun i => by simp⟩
  | add x y _ _ hx hy =>
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hx
    obtain ⟨c', hc'⟩ := hy
    exact ⟨c + c', fun i => by simp [Finset.sum_add_distrib, hc, hc', add_smul]⟩
  | neg x _ hx =>
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hx
    exact ⟨-c, fun i => by simp [hc, neg_smul]⟩

/-- The homomorphism `c ↦ (∑ j ∈ U i, c j)_{i ∈ I}`. -/
private def sumsHom {p : ℕ} (U : Fin p → Finset ι) (I : Finset (Fin p)) : (ι → G) →+ (I → G) where
  toFun c i := ∑ j ∈ U i, c j
  map_zero' := by funext i; simp
  map_add' c c' := by funext i; simp [Finset.sum_add_distrib]

omit [Fintype G] [DecidableEq G] [Fintype ι] in
private lemma sumsHom_surjective {p : ℕ} (U : Fin p → Finset ι) {I : Finset (Fin p)}
    (hI : Spans (AddSubgroup.closure (Set.range fun j => ind (rowSet U j))) I) :
    Function.Surjective (sumsHom (G := G) U I) := by
  intro w
  have key : ∀ i₀ : I, ∃ c : ι → G, sumsHom U I c = Pi.single i₀ (w i₀) := by
    intro i₀
    obtain ⟨y, hy, hyz⟩ := hI (ind {(i₀ : Fin p)})
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := exists_sum_eq_smul U hy (w i₀)
    refine ⟨c, funext fun i => ?_⟩
    change ∑ j ∈ U i, c j = _
    rw [hc, hyz i i.2]
    by_cases h : i = i₀
    · subst h; simp [ind]
    · have : (i : Fin p) ≠ i₀ := fun h' => h (Subtype.ext h')
      simp [ind, this, h]
  choose c hc using key
  exact ⟨∑ i₀, c i₀, by rw [map_sum]; simp only [hc]; exact Finset.univ_sum_single w⟩

private lemma card_sums_mem_mul_le {p : ℕ} (U : Fin p → Finset ι) {I : Finset (Fin p)}
    (hI : Spans (AddSubgroup.closure (Set.range fun j => ind (rowSet U j))) I) (B : Finset G) :
    #{c : ι → G | ∀ i, ∑ j ∈ U i, c j ∈ B} * Fintype.card G ^ #I ≤
      #B ^ #I * Fintype.card G ^ Fintype.card ι := by
  set φ := sumsHom (G := G) U I
  have hφ := sumsHom_surjective (G := G) U hI
  have hF := card_fiber_mul_card φ hφ 0
  rw [Fintype.card_fun, Fintype.card_fun, Fintype.card_coe] at hF
  have h1 : #{c : ι → G | ∀ i, ∑ j ∈ U i, c j ∈ B} ≤
      #{c : ι → G | φ c ∈ Fintype.piFinset fun _ => B} := by
    refine card_le_card fun c hc => ?_
    simp only [mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and, Fintype.mem_piFinset] at hc ⊢
    exact fun i => hc i
  have h2 : #{c : ι → G | φ c ∈ Fintype.piFinset fun _ => B} =
      ∑ w ∈ Fintype.piFinset (fun _ : I => B), #{c | φ c = w} := by
    rw [card_eq_sum_card_fiberwise (f := φ) (fun c hc => mem_coe.2 (mem_filter.1 (mem_coe.1 hc)).2)]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun w hw => ?_
    congr 1; ext c; simp only [mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and]
    constructor
    · exact fun h => h.2
    · intro h; exact ⟨h ▸ hw, h⟩
  have h3 : ∀ w, #{c | φ c = w} = #{c | φ c = 0} := fun w =>
    AddMonoidHom.card_fiber_eq_of_mem_range φ (hφ w) (hφ 0)
  rw [h2, Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun w _ => h3 w), sum_const, Fintype.card_piFinset,
    prod_const, card_univ, Fintype.card_coe, smul_eq_mul] at h1
  calc #{c : ι → G | ∀ i, ∑ j ∈ U i, c j ∈ B} * Fintype.card G ^ #I
      ≤ #B ^ #I * #{c | φ c = 0} * Fintype.card G ^ #I := Nat.mul_le_mul_right _ h1
    _ = #B ^ #I * Fintype.card G ^ Fintype.card ι := by rw [mul_assoc, hF]

/-- Number of subsets of the index set whose sum lies in `B`. -/
private def hit (B : Finset G) (c : ι → G) : ℕ := #{s : Finset ι | ∑ j ∈ s, c j ∈ B}

/-- The set of row types of `U`. -/
private def typeSet {p : ℕ} (U : Fin p → Finset ι) : Finset (Finset (Fin p)) :=
  univ.image (rowSet U)

/-- The subgroup of `ℤ^p` generated by the indicator vectors of `T`. -/
private def latticeOf {p : ℕ} (T : Finset (Finset (Fin p))) : AddSubgroup (Fin p → ℤ) :=
  AddSubgroup.closure (ind '' (T : Set (Finset (Fin p))))

/-- A set of coordinates onto which `latticeOf T` projects, with `#T ≤ 2 ^ #(spanSet T)`. -/
private noncomputable def spanSet {p : ℕ} (T : Finset (Finset (Fin p))) : Finset (Fin p) :=
  Classical.choose (lattice_count (univ : Finset (Fin p)) (latticeOf T) 0)

private lemma spanSet_spec {p : ℕ} (T : Finset (Finset (Fin p))) :
    Spans (latticeOf T) (spanSet T) ∧ #T ≤ 2 ^ #(spanSet T) := by
  have h := Classical.choose_spec (lattice_count (univ : Finset (Fin p)) (latticeOf T) 0)
  refine ⟨h.1, le_trans (card_le_card ?_) h.2⟩
  intro τ hτ
  simp only [mem_filter, mem_powerset, subset_univ, true_and, sub_zero]
  exact AddSubgroup.subset_closure ⟨τ, hτ, rfl⟩

omit [Fintype G] [DecidableEq G] in
private lemma closure_rowSet {p : ℕ} (U : Fin p → Finset ι) :
    AddSubgroup.closure (Set.range fun j => ind (rowSet U j)) = latticeOf (typeSet U) := by
  unfold latticeOf typeSet
  rw [coe_image, coe_univ, Set.image_univ, ← Set.range_comp]
  rfl

omit [Fintype G] [DecidableEq G] in
private lemma card_typeSet_eq_le {p : ℕ} (T : Finset (Finset (Fin p))) :
    #{U : Fin p → Finset ι | typeSet U = T} ≤ #T ^ Fintype.card ι := by
  calc #{U : Fin p → Finset ι | typeSet U = T}
      ≤ #(Fintype.piFinset fun _ : ι => T) := by
        refine card_le_card_of_injOn (fun U => rowSet U) ?_ ?_
        · intro U hU
          simp only [coe_filter, mem_univ, true_and, Set.mem_ofPred_eq] at hU
          rw [mem_coe, Fintype.mem_piFinset]
          intro j
          rw [← hU]
          exact mem_image_of_mem _ (mem_univ j)
        · intro U _ U' _ h
          funext i
          ext j
          have := congrArg (fun r => i ∈ r) (congrFun h j)
          simpa [rowSet] using this
    _ = #T ^ Fintype.card ι := by rw [Fintype.card_piFinset, prod_const, card_univ]

/-- **High-moment bound for the hitting count.** -/
private theorem sum_hit_pow_le (B : Finset G) (p : ℕ) :
    ∑ c : ι → G, (hit B c : ℝ) ^ p ≤
      2 ^ 2 ^ p * (Fintype.card G : ℝ) ^ Fintype.card ι *
        max 1 ((2 : ℝ) ^ Fintype.card ι * #B / Fintype.card G) ^ p := by
  set N := Fintype.card G
  set m := Fintype.card ι
  have hN : (0 : ℝ) < N := by exact_mod_cast Fintype.card_pos
  have expand : ∀ c : ι → G, (hit B c : ℝ) ^ p =
      ∑ U : Fin p → Finset ι, ∏ i, (if ∑ j ∈ U i, c j ∈ B then (1 : ℝ) else 0) := by
    intro c
    have : (hit B c : ℝ) = ∑ s : Finset ι, (if ∑ j ∈ s, c j ∈ B then (1 : ℝ) else 0) := by
      simp only [hit, Finset.card_filter, Nat.cast_sum, Nat.cast_ite, Nat.cast_one,
        Nat.cast_zero]
    rw [this, ← Fin.prod_const, Finset.prod_univ_sum, Fintype.piFinset_univ]
  have hZ : ∀ U : Fin p → Finset ι,
      ∑ c : ι → G, ∏ i, (if ∑ j ∈ U i, c j ∈ B then (1 : ℝ) else 0) =
        #{c : ι → G | ∀ i, ∑ j ∈ U i, c j ∈ B} := by
    intro U
    simp only [Finset.prod_boole, mem_univ, true_implies]
    rw [Finset.sum_boole]
  have perT : ∀ T : Finset (Finset (Fin p)),
      ∑ U ∈ {U : Fin p → Finset ι | typeSet U = T}, (#{c : ι → G | ∀ i, ∑ j ∈ U i, c j ∈ B} : ℝ)
        ≤ (N : ℝ) ^ m * max 1 ((2 : ℝ) ^ m * #B / N) ^ p := by
    intro T
    obtain ⟨hI, hT⟩ := spanSet_spec T
    set k := #(spanSet T)
    have hU : ∀ U ∈ ({U : Fin p → Finset ι | typeSet U = T} : Finset _),
        (#{c : ι → G | ∀ i, ∑ j ∈ U i, c j ∈ B} : ℝ) ≤ #B ^ k * N ^ m / N ^ k := by
      intro U hU
      simp only [mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and] at hU
      have h := card_sums_mem_mul_le (G := G) U (I := spanSet T)
        (by rw [closure_rowSet, hU]; exact hI) B
      rw [le_div_iff₀ (pow_pos hN _)]
      exact_mod_cast h
    calc ∑ U ∈ {U : Fin p → Finset ι | typeSet U = T}, (#{c : ι → G | ∀ i, ∑ j ∈ U i, c j ∈ B} : ℝ)
        ≤ ∑ U ∈ {U : Fin p → Finset ι | typeSet U = T}, ((#B : ℝ) ^ k * N ^ m / N ^ k) :=
          sum_le_sum hU
      _ = #{U : Fin p → Finset ι | typeSet U = T} * ((#B : ℝ) ^ k * N ^ m / N ^ k) := by
          rw [sum_const, nsmul_eq_mul]
      _ ≤ ((2 : ℝ) ^ k) ^ m * ((#B : ℝ) ^ k * N ^ m / N ^ k) := by
          gcongr
          calc (#{U : Fin p → Finset ι | typeSet U = T} : ℝ) ≤ (#T : ℝ) ^ m := by
                exact_mod_cast card_typeSet_eq_le T
            _ ≤ ((2 : ℝ) ^ k) ^ m := by gcongr; exact_mod_cast hT
      _ = (N : ℝ) ^ m * ((2 : ℝ) ^ m * #B / N) ^ k := by
          have hNk : (N : ℝ) ^ k ≠ 0 := by positivity
          rw [div_pow, mul_pow, ← pow_mul, ← pow_mul, mul_comm m k]
          field_simp
      _ ≤ (N : ℝ) ^ m * max 1 ((2 : ℝ) ^ m * #B / N) ^ p := by
          gcongr
          have hx : (0 : ℝ) ≤ (2 : ℝ) ^ m * #B / N := by positivity
          calc ((2 : ℝ) ^ m * #B / N) ^ k ≤ (max 1 ((2 : ℝ) ^ m * #B / N)) ^ k :=
                pow_le_pow_left₀ hx (le_max_right _ _) k
            _ ≤ max 1 ((2 : ℝ) ^ m * #B / N) ^ p :=
                pow_le_pow_right₀ (le_max_left _ _) (by
                  calc k ≤ #(univ : Finset (Fin p)) := card_le_card (subset_univ _)
                    _ = p := by simp)
  calc ∑ c : ι → G, (hit B c : ℝ) ^ p
      = ∑ U : Fin p → Finset ι, (#{c : ι → G | ∀ i, ∑ j ∈ U i, c j ∈ B} : ℝ) := by
        simp_rw [expand]
        rw [Finset.sum_comm]
        exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun U _ => hZ U
    _ = ∑ T : Finset (Finset (Fin p)), ∑ U ∈ {U : Fin p → Finset ι | typeSet U = T},
          (#{c : ι → G | ∀ i, ∑ j ∈ U i, c j ∈ B} : ℝ) :=
        (Finset.sum_fiberwise _ _ _).symm
    _ ≤ ∑ _T : Finset (Finset (Fin p)), (N : ℝ) ^ m * max 1 ((2 : ℝ) ^ m * #B / N) ^ p :=
        sum_le_sum fun T _ => perT T
    _ = 2 ^ 2 ^ p * (N : ℝ) ^ m * max 1 ((2 : ℝ) ^ m * #B / N) ^ p := by
        rw [sum_const, card_univ, Fintype.card_finset, Fintype.card_finset, Fintype.card_fin,
          nsmul_eq_mul]
        push_cast
        ring

/-! ### Subset-sum counts of tuples and their second moment -/

/-- Number of subsets of the index set whose sum is `g`. -/
private def cnt (f : ι → G) (g : G) : ℕ := #{s : Finset ι | ∑ j ∈ s, f j = g}

omit [DecidableEq ι] in
private lemma sum_cnt (f : ι → G) : ∑ g, cnt f g = 2 ^ Fintype.card ι := by
  rw [← Fintype.card_finset, ← card_univ]
  exact (card_eq_sum_card_fiberwise (f := fun s => ∑ j ∈ s, f j)
    (fun _ _ => mem_coe.2 (mem_univ _))).symm

omit [DecidableEq ι] in
private lemma sum_cnt_sq (f : ι → G) :
    ∑ g, cnt f g ^ 2 = #{x : Finset ι × Finset ι | ∑ j ∈ x.1, f j = ∑ j ∈ x.2, f j} := by
  rw [card_eq_sum_card_fiberwise (f := fun x : Finset ι × Finset ι => ∑ j ∈ x.1, f j)
    (t := univ) (fun _ _ => mem_coe.2 (mem_univ _))]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun g _ => ?_
  rw [sq, cnt, ← card_product, filter_filter]
  congr 1
  ext x
  simp only [mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and, mem_product]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨h1, h2⟩; exact ⟨h1.trans h2.symm, h1⟩
  · rintro ⟨h1, h2⟩; exact ⟨h2, h1 ▸ h2⟩

/-- `c ↦ ∑ j ∈ s, c j - ∑ j ∈ t, c j`. -/
private def diffHom (s t : Finset ι) : (ι → G) →+ G where
  toFun c := ∑ j ∈ s, c j - ∑ j ∈ t, c j
  map_zero' := by simp
  map_add' c c' := by simp [Finset.sum_add_distrib]; abel

omit [Fintype G] [DecidableEq G] [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] in
private lemma diffHom_surjective {s t : Finset ι} (hst : s ≠ t) :
    Function.Surjective (diffHom (G := G) s t) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ : ∃ j, ¬ (j ∈ s ↔ j ∈ t) := by
    by_contra h
    push Not at h
    exact hst (Finset.ext h)
  intro g
  by_cases hs : j ∈ s
  · have ht : j ∉ t := fun h => hj ⟨fun _ => h, fun _ => hs⟩
    exact ⟨Pi.single j g, by simp [diffHom, Finset.sum_pi_single', hs, ht]⟩
  · have ht : j ∈ t := by tauto
    exact ⟨Pi.single j (-g), by simp [diffHom, Finset.sum_pi_single', hs, ht]⟩

/-- **Second moment.** -/
private theorem sum_sum_cnt_sub_sq (k : ℕ) (hk : Fintype.card ι = k) :
    ∑ f : ι → G, ∑ g, ((cnt f g : ℝ) - 2 ^ k / Fintype.card G) ^ 2 ≤
      2 ^ k * (Fintype.card G : ℝ) ^ k := by
  subst hk
  set N := Fintype.card G
  set m := Fintype.card ι
  have hN : (0 : ℝ) < N := by exact_mod_cast Fintype.card_pos
  have h1 : ∀ f : ι → G, ∑ g, ((cnt f g : ℝ) - 2 ^ m / N) ^ 2 =
      (#{x : Finset ι × Finset ι | ∑ j ∈ x.1, f j = ∑ j ∈ x.2, f j} : ℝ) - 4 ^ m / N := by
    intro f
    have hs : ∑ g, (cnt f g : ℝ) = 2 ^ m := by exact_mod_cast sum_cnt f
    have hs2 : ∑ g, (cnt f g : ℝ) ^ 2 =
        #{x : Finset ι × Finset ι | ∑ j ∈ x.1, f j = ∑ j ∈ x.2, f j} := by
      exact_mod_cast sum_cnt_sq f
    simp only [sub_sq, sum_add_distrib, sum_sub_distrib, ← sum_mul, ← mul_sum, hs, hs2, sum_const,
      card_univ, nsmul_eq_mul]
    rw [show (4 : ℝ) ^ m = (2 ^ m) ^ 2 by rw [← pow_mul, mul_comm, pow_mul]; norm_num]
    field_simp
    ring
  have h2 : ∀ x : Finset ι × Finset ι,
      (#{f : ι → G | ∑ j ∈ x.1, f j = ∑ j ∈ x.2, f j} : ℝ) ≤
        (if x.1 = x.2 then (N : ℝ) ^ m else 0) + (N : ℝ) ^ m / N := by
    intro x
    by_cases hx : x.1 = x.2
    · rw [ite_eq_left hx]
      have : (#{f : ι → G | ∑ j ∈ x.1, f j = ∑ j ∈ x.2, f j} : ℝ) ≤ (N : ℝ) ^ m := by
        have := card_le_univ ({f : ι → G | ∑ j ∈ x.1, f j = ∑ j ∈ x.2, f j} : Finset _)
        rw [Fintype.card_fun] at this
        exact_mod_cast this
      linarith [div_nonneg (pow_nonneg hN.le m) hN.le]
    · rw [ite_eq_right hx, zero_add, le_div_iff₀ hN]
      have h := card_fiber_mul_card (diffHom (G := G) x.1 x.2) (diffHom_surjective hx) 0
      rw [Fintype.card_fun] at h
      have he : ({f : ι → G | ∑ j ∈ x.1, f j = ∑ j ∈ x.2, f j} : Finset _) =
          ({f | diffHom (G := G) x.1 x.2 f = 0} : Finset (ι → G)) := by
        ext f; simp [diffHom, sub_eq_zero]
      rw [he]
      exact_mod_cast h.le
  have hdiag : #{x : Finset ι × Finset ι | x.1 = x.2} = 2 ^ m := by
    rw [← Fintype.card_finset, ← card_univ]
    refine card_bij (fun x _ => x.1) (fun _ _ => mem_univ _) ?_ ?_
    · intro x hx y hy hxy
      simp only [mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and] at hx hy
      exact Prod.ext hxy (hx ▸ hy ▸ hxy)
    · intro s _
      exact ⟨(s, s), by simp, rfl⟩
  calc ∑ f : ι → G, ∑ g, ((cnt f g : ℝ) - 2 ^ m / N) ^ 2
      = ∑ f : ι → G, ((#{x : Finset ι × Finset ι | ∑ j ∈ x.1, f j = ∑ j ∈ x.2, f j} : ℝ)
          - 4 ^ m / N) := Finset.sum_congr rfl fun f _ => h1 f
    _ = ∑ x : Finset ι × Finset ι, (#{f : ι → G | ∑ j ∈ x.1, f j = ∑ j ∈ x.2, f j} : ℝ)
          - N ^ m * (4 ^ m / N) := by
        rw [sum_sub_distrib, sum_const, card_univ, Fintype.card_fun, nsmul_eq_mul]
        congr 1
        · simp only [card_filter, Nat.cast_sum, Nat.cast_ite, Nat.cast_one, Nat.cast_zero]
          exact Finset.sum_comm
        · push_cast; ring
    _ ≤ ∑ x : Finset ι × Finset ι, ((if x.1 = x.2 then (N : ℝ) ^ m else 0) + (N : ℝ) ^ m / N)
          - N ^ m * (4 ^ m / N) := by gcongr with x; exact h2 x
    _ = 2 ^ m * (N : ℝ) ^ m - 0 := by
        rw [sum_add_distrib, sum_ite, sum_const_zero, add_zero, sum_const, sum_const, card_univ,
          Fintype.card_prod, Fintype.card_finset, nsmul_eq_mul, nsmul_eq_mul]
        rw [show ({x ∈ (univ : Finset (Finset ι × Finset ι)) | x.1 = x.2}) =
          ({x : Finset ι × Finset ι | x.1 = x.2} : Finset _) from rfl, hdiag]
        push_cast
        rw [show (4 : ℝ) ^ m = 2 ^ m * 2 ^ m by rw [← mul_pow]; norm_num]
        ring
    _ = 2 ^ m * (N : ℝ) ^ m := sub_zero _

section Split

variable {ι₁ ι₂ : Type*} [Fintype ι₁] [Fintype ι₂] [DecidableEq ι₁] [DecidableEq ι₂]

omit [DecidableEq ι] [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι₁] [DecidableEq ι₂] in
/-- Subset sums of a concatenated tuple: convolution of the two counts. -/
private lemma cnt_sumElim (a : ι₁ → G) (c : ι₂ → G) (g : G) :
    cnt (Sum.elim a c) g = ∑ h, cnt a h * cnt c (g - h) := by
  have e1 : cnt (Sum.elim a c) g =
      #{x : Finset ι₁ × Finset ι₂ | ∑ j ∈ x.1, a j + ∑ j ∈ x.2, c j = g} := by
    unfold cnt
    refine Finset.card_equiv Finset.sumEquiv.toEquiv fun u => ?_
    change _ ↔ (u.toLeft, u.toRight) ∈ _
    simp only [mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and]
    rw [Finset.sum_sum_eq_sum_toLeft_add_sum_toRight]
    simp
  rw [e1, card_eq_sum_card_fiberwise (f := fun x : Finset ι₁ × Finset ι₂ => ∑ j ∈ x.1, a j)
    (t := univ) (fun _ _ => mem_coe.2 (mem_univ _))]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun h _ => ?_
  rw [cnt, cnt, ← card_product, filter_filter]
  congr 1
  ext x
  simp only [mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and, mem_product]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨e, h1⟩
    exact ⟨h1, by rw [← h1, ← e]; abel⟩
  · rintro ⟨h1, h2⟩
    exact ⟨by rw [h1, h2]; abel, h1⟩

omit [Fintype G] [DecidableEq ι] [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι₁] [DecidableEq ι₂] in
/-- **Deterministic stage-two estimate.** -/
private lemma abs_cnt_sumElim_sub_le [Finite G] (a : ι₁ → G) (c : ι₂ → G) (μ₁ η K : ℝ)
    (B : Finset G) (hη : 0 ≤ η) (hB : ∀ h ∉ B, |(cnt a h : ℝ) - μ₁| ≤ η)
    (hK : ∀ h, |(cnt a h : ℝ) - μ₁| ≤ K) (g : G) :
    |(cnt (Sum.elim a c) g : ℝ) - 2 ^ Fintype.card ι₂ * μ₁| ≤
      2 ^ Fintype.card ι₂ * η + K * #{t : Finset ι₂ | g - ∑ j ∈ t, c j ∈ B} := by
  have := Fintype.ofFinite G
  have hsum : ∑ h, (cnt c (g - h) : ℝ) = 2 ^ Fintype.card ι₂ := by
    rw [show ∑ h, (cnt c (g - h) : ℝ) = ∑ h, (cnt c h : ℝ) from
      Fintype.sum_equiv (Equiv.subLeft g) _ _ (fun h => rfl)]
    exact_mod_cast sum_cnt c
  have hB' : ∑ h ∈ B, (cnt c (g - h) : ℝ) = #{t : Finset ι₂ | g - ∑ j ∈ t, c j ∈ B} := by
    rw [card_eq_sum_card_fiberwise (f := fun t : Finset ι₂ => g - ∑ j ∈ t, c j) (t := B)
      (fun t ht => mem_coe.2 (mem_filter.1 (mem_coe.1 ht)).2)]
    push_cast
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun h hh => ?_
    rw [cnt]
    congr 2
    ext t
    simp only [mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and]
    constructor
    · intro e
      have e' : g - ∑ j ∈ t, c j = h := by rw [e]; abel
      exact ⟨e' ▸ hh, e'⟩
    · rintro ⟨_, e⟩
      rw [← e]; abel
  calc |(cnt (Sum.elim a c) g : ℝ) - 2 ^ Fintype.card ι₂ * μ₁|
      = |∑ h, (cnt c (g - h) : ℝ) * ((cnt a h : ℝ) - μ₁)| := by
        congr 1
        rw [cnt_sumElim]
        push_cast
        rw [← hsum, Finset.sum_mul, ← Finset.sum_sub_distrib]
        refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun h _ => ?_
        ring
    _ ≤ ∑ h, (cnt c (g - h) : ℝ) * |(cnt a h : ℝ) - μ₁| := by
        refine (abs_sum_le_sum_abs _ _).trans (le_of_eq ?_)
        refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun h _ => ?_
        rw [abs_mul, Nat.abs_cast]
    _ ≤ ∑ h, (cnt c (g - h) : ℝ) * (η + if h ∈ B then K else 0) := by
        gcongr with h
        by_cases hh : h ∈ B
        · rw [ite_eq_left hh]; linarith [hK h]
        · rw [ite_eq_right hh, add_zero]; exact hB h hh
    _ = 2 ^ Fintype.card ι₂ * η + K * #{t : Finset ι₂ | g - ∑ j ∈ t, c j ∈ B} := by
        simp only [mul_add, sum_add_distrib, ← sum_mul, hsum, mul_ite, mul_zero]
        rw [Finset.sum_ite_mem, univ_inter, ← sum_mul, hB']
        ring

end Split

omit [AddCommGroup G] [DecidableEq G] [DecidableEq ι] [Fintype ι] in
/-! ### The two stages -/

/-- Markov's inequality for a finite sum. -/
private lemma card_le_sum_div {α : Type*} [Fintype α] (F : α → ℝ) (hF : ∀ x, 0 ≤ F x) {T : ℝ}
    (hT : 0 < T) : (#{x | T ≤ F x} : ℝ) ≤ (∑ x, F x) / T := by
  rw [le_div_iff₀ hT]
  calc (#{x | T ≤ F x} : ℝ) * T = ∑ x ∈ ({x | T ≤ F x} : Finset α), T := by
        rw [sum_const, nsmul_eq_mul]
    _ ≤ ∑ x ∈ ({x | T ≤ F x} : Finset α), F x := sum_le_sum fun x hx => (mem_filter.1 hx).2
    _ ≤ ∑ x, F x := sum_le_sum_of_subset_of_nonneg (subset_univ _) fun x _ _ => hF x

omit [Fintype G] [DecidableEq ι] in
private lemma hit_singleton (c : ι → G) (h : G) : hit {h} c = cnt c h := by
  simp [hit, cnt]

omit [Fintype G] [DecidableEq ι] in
private lemma hit_image_sub (B : Finset G) (c : ι → G) (g : G) :
    hit (B.image (g - ·)) c = #{t : Finset ι | g - ∑ j ∈ t, c j ∈ B} := by
  unfold hit
  congr 1
  ext t
  simp only [mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and, mem_image]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨h, hh, e⟩; rw [← e]; simpa using hh
  · intro ht; exact ⟨g - ∑ j ∈ t, c j, ht, by abel⟩

/-- The subset-sum counts of the tuple `f` are `ε`-balanced. -/
private def Bal (ε : ℝ) (f : ι → G) : Prop :=
  ∀ g, |(cnt f g : ℝ) - 2 ^ Fintype.card ι / Fintype.card G| ≤
    ε * (2 ^ Fintype.card ι / Fintype.card G)

/-- **Stage one.** Few tuples have a large quadratic deviation or a large count. -/
private lemma card_not_good_le (k₁ p : ℕ) (hk₁ : Fintype.card ι = k₁) {K t : ℝ} (hK : 1 ≤ K)
    (ht : 0 < t) (hKp : (Fintype.card G : ℝ) ^ 2 ≤ K ^ p)
    (hμ : (Fintype.card G : ℝ) ≤ 2 ^ k₁) :
    (#{a : ι → G | ¬ ((∑ h, ((cnt a h : ℝ) - 2 ^ k₁ / Fintype.card G) ^ 2 ≤ t * 2 ^ k₁) ∧
        ∀ h, (cnt a h : ℝ) ≤ K * (2 ^ k₁ / Fintype.card G))} : ℝ) ≤
      (Fintype.card G : ℝ) ^ k₁ / t + 2 ^ 2 ^ p * (Fintype.card G : ℝ) ^ k₁ / Fintype.card G := by
  classical
  set N := Fintype.card G
  set μ₁ : ℝ := 2 ^ k₁ / N with hμ₁def
  have hN : (0 : ℝ) < N := by exact_mod_cast Fintype.card_pos
  have hμ₁ : 1 ≤ μ₁ := by rw [hμ₁def, le_div_iff₀ hN, one_mul]; exact hμ
  have hsub : ({a : ι → G | ¬ ((∑ h, ((cnt a h : ℝ) - μ₁) ^ 2 ≤ t * 2 ^ k₁) ∧
        ∀ h, (cnt a h : ℝ) ≤ K * μ₁)} : Finset _) ⊆
      ({a | t * 2 ^ k₁ ≤ ∑ h, ((cnt a h : ℝ) - μ₁) ^ 2} : Finset _) ∪
        univ.biUnion (fun h => ({a | (K * μ₁) ^ p ≤ (cnt a h : ℝ) ^ p} : Finset _)) := by
    intro a ha
    simp only [mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and, not_and_or, not_le, not_forall] at ha
    rcases ha with h1 | ⟨h, h2⟩
    · exact mem_union_left _ (by simp only [mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and]; exact h1.le)
    · refine mem_union_right _ (mem_biUnion.2 ⟨h, mem_univ _, ?_⟩)
      simp only [mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and]
      exact pow_le_pow_left₀ (by positivity) h2.le p
  have hmom : ∀ h : G, ∑ a : ι → G, (cnt a h : ℝ) ^ p ≤ 2 ^ 2 ^ p * (N : ℝ) ^ k₁ * μ₁ ^ p := by
    intro h
    have := sum_hit_pow_le (ι := ι) ({h} : Finset G) p
    simp only [hit_singleton, card_singleton, Nat.cast_one, mul_one, hk₁] at this
    rwa [max_eq_right hμ₁] at this
  calc (#{a : ι → G | ¬ ((∑ h, ((cnt a h : ℝ) - μ₁) ^ 2 ≤ t * 2 ^ k₁) ∧
        ∀ h, (cnt a h : ℝ) ≤ K * μ₁)} : ℝ)
      ≤ (#({a | t * 2 ^ k₁ ≤ ∑ h, ((cnt a h : ℝ) - μ₁) ^ 2} : Finset (ι → G)) : ℝ) +
          ∑ h : G, (#({a | (K * μ₁) ^ p ≤ (cnt a h : ℝ) ^ p} : Finset (ι → G)) : ℝ) := by
        have h1 := card_le_card hsub
        have h2 := card_union_le ({a | t * 2 ^ k₁ ≤ ∑ h, ((cnt a h : ℝ) - μ₁) ^ 2} : Finset (ι → G))
          (univ.biUnion (fun h => ({a | (K * μ₁) ^ p ≤ (cnt a h : ℝ) ^ p} : Finset _)))
        have h3 := card_biUnion_le (s := (univ : Finset G))
          (t := fun h => ({a | (K * μ₁) ^ p ≤ (cnt a h : ℝ) ^ p} : Finset (ι → G)))
        exact_mod_cast h1.trans (h2.trans (Nat.add_le_add_left h3 _))
    _ ≤ (2 ^ k₁ * (N : ℝ) ^ k₁) / (t * 2 ^ k₁) +
          ∑ h : G, (∑ a : ι → G, (cnt a h : ℝ) ^ p) / (K * μ₁) ^ p := by
        gcongr with h
        · exact (card_le_sum_div _ (fun a => sum_nonneg fun h _ => sq_nonneg _)
            (by positivity)).trans (div_le_div_of_nonneg_right
              (sum_sum_cnt_sub_sq k₁ hk₁) (by positivity))
        · exact card_le_sum_div _ (fun a => by positivity) (by positivity)
    _ ≤ (N : ℝ) ^ k₁ / t + ∑ _h : G, 2 ^ 2 ^ p * (N : ℝ) ^ k₁ * μ₁ ^ p / (K * μ₁) ^ p := by
        have e : (2 ^ k₁ * (N : ℝ) ^ k₁) / (t * 2 ^ k₁) = (N : ℝ) ^ k₁ / t := by field_simp
        rw [e]
        gcongr with h
        exact hmom h
    _ = (N : ℝ) ^ k₁ / t + N * (2 ^ 2 ^ p * (N : ℝ) ^ k₁ / K ^ p) := by
        rw [sum_const, card_univ, nsmul_eq_mul, mul_pow]
        congr 2
        field_simp
    _ ≤ (N : ℝ) ^ k₁ / t + 2 ^ 2 ^ p * (N : ℝ) ^ k₁ / N := by
        gcongr
        rw [mul_div_assoc', div_le_div_iff₀ (by positivity) hN]
        calc (N : ℝ) * (2 ^ 2 ^ p * N ^ k₁) * N = 2 ^ 2 ^ p * N ^ k₁ * N ^ 2 := by ring
          _ ≤ 2 ^ 2 ^ p * N ^ k₁ * K ^ p := by gcongr

section Split2

variable {ι₁ ι₂ : Type*} [Fintype ι₁] [Fintype ι₂] [DecidableEq ι₁] [DecidableEq ι₂]

omit [DecidableEq ι₁] in
open scoped Classical in
/-- **Stage two.** For a good first block, few second blocks spoil the balance. -/
private lemma card_not_bal_le (a : ι₁ → G) (k₁ m p : ℕ) (hk₁ : Fintype.card ι₁ = k₁)
    (hm : Fintype.card ι₂ = m) {ε K t : ℝ} (hε : 0 < ε) (hK : 1 ≤ K) (ht : 0 < t)
    (hKp : (Fintype.card G : ℝ) ^ 2 ≤ K ^ p) (hm' : 2 * K ^ 2 ≤ 2 ^ m * ε)
    (hk' : 8 * t * K ^ 2 * Fintype.card G ≤ 2 ^ k₁ * ε ^ 3)
    (hD : ∑ h, ((cnt a h : ℝ) - 2 ^ k₁ / Fintype.card G) ^ 2 ≤ t * 2 ^ k₁)
    (hmax : ∀ h, (cnt a h : ℝ) ≤ K * (2 ^ k₁ / Fintype.card G)) :
    (#{c : ι₂ → G | ¬ Bal ε (Sum.elim a c)} : ℝ) ≤
      2 ^ 2 ^ p * (Fintype.card G : ℝ) ^ m / Fintype.card G := by
  classical
  set N := Fintype.card G
  set μ₁ : ℝ := 2 ^ k₁ / N with hμ₁def
  have hN : (0 : ℝ) < N := by exact_mod_cast Fintype.card_pos
  have hμ₁ : 0 < μ₁ := by positivity
  set η : ℝ := ε / 2 * μ₁ with hηdef
  have hη : 0 < η := by positivity
  set B : Finset G := {h | η < |(cnt a h : ℝ) - μ₁|} with hBdef
  set lam : ℝ := ε / 2 * 2 ^ m / K with hlam
  have hlam0 : 0 < lam := by positivity
  have hB : ∀ h ∉ B, |(cnt a h : ℝ) - μ₁| ≤ η := fun h hh => by
    simpa [hBdef] using hh
  have hKabs : ∀ h, |(cnt a h : ℝ) - μ₁| ≤ K * μ₁ := fun h => by
    rw [abs_le]
    constructor
    · nlinarith [Nat.cast_nonneg (α := ℝ) (cnt a h)]
    · linarith [hmax h]
  -- the exceptional set is small
  have hBcard : (#B : ℝ) ≤ t * 2 ^ k₁ / η ^ 2 := by
    have hsub : B ⊆ ({h | η ^ 2 ≤ ((cnt a h : ℝ) - μ₁) ^ 2} : Finset G) := by
      intro h hh
      simp only [hBdef, mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and] at hh ⊢
      rw [← sq_abs ((cnt a h : ℝ) - μ₁)]
      exact pow_le_pow_left₀ hη.le hh.le 2
    calc (#B : ℝ) ≤ #({h | η ^ 2 ≤ ((cnt a h : ℝ) - μ₁) ^ 2} : Finset G) := by
          exact_mod_cast card_le_card hsub
      _ ≤ (∑ h, ((cnt a h : ℝ) - μ₁) ^ 2) / η ^ 2 :=
          card_le_sum_div _ (fun h => sq_nonneg _) (by positivity)
      _ ≤ t * 2 ^ k₁ / η ^ 2 := by gcongr
  -- a spoiled second block makes some hitting count large
  have hsub : ({c : ι₂ → G | ¬ Bal ε (Sum.elim a c)} : Finset _) ⊆
      univ.biUnion (fun g => ({c | lam ^ p ≤ (hit (B.image (g - ·)) c : ℝ) ^ p} : Finset _)) := by
    intro c hc
    simp only [Bal, mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and, not_forall, not_le] at hc
    obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := hc
    refine mem_biUnion.2 ⟨g, mem_univ _, ?_⟩
    simp only [mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and]
    refine pow_le_pow_left₀ hlam0.le ?_ p
    have h2 := abs_cnt_sumElim_sub_le a c μ₁ η (K * μ₁) B hη.le hB hKabs g
    rw [hit_image_sub]
    have hcard : (2 : ℝ) ^ Fintype.card (ι₁ ⊕ ι₂) / N = 2 ^ m * μ₁ := by
      rw [Fintype.card_sum, hk₁, hm, pow_add, hμ₁def]; ring
    rw [hcard] at hg
    rw [hm] at h2
    set H : ℝ := (#{t : Finset ι₂ | g - ∑ j ∈ t, c j ∈ B} : ℝ)
    have : ε / 2 * (2 ^ m * μ₁) ≤ K * μ₁ * H := by
      rw [hηdef] at h2
      nlinarith
    rw [hlam, div_le_iff₀ (by positivity)]
    nlinarith
  have hratio : max 1 ((2 : ℝ) ^ m * #B / N) / lam ≤ 1 / K := by
    rw [div_le_div_iff₀ hlam0 (by positivity), one_mul, max_mul_of_nonneg _ _ (by positivity),
      max_le_iff]
    have hK0 : 0 < K := by linarith
    constructor
    · rw [one_mul, hlam, le_div_iff₀ hK0]
      nlinarith
    · calc (2 : ℝ) ^ m * #B / N * K ≤ 2 ^ m * (t * 2 ^ k₁ / η ^ 2) / N * K := by gcongr
        _ ≤ lam := by
          rw [hlam, hηdef, hμ₁def]
          have e : (2 : ℝ) ^ m * (t * 2 ^ k₁ / (ε / 2 * (2 ^ k₁ / N)) ^ 2) / N * K =
              4 * t * 2 ^ m * N * K / (ε ^ 2 * 2 ^ k₁) := by
            field_simp
            ring
          rw [e, div_le_div_iff₀ (by positivity) hK0]
          have h2m : (0 : ℝ) ≤ 2 ^ m / 2 := by positivity
          have := mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left hk' h2m
          nlinarith
  have hmom : ∀ g : G, (∑ c : ι₂ → G, (hit (B.image (g - ·)) c : ℝ) ^ p) / lam ^ p ≤
      2 ^ 2 ^ p * (N : ℝ) ^ m / K ^ p := by
    intro g
    have h1 := sum_hit_pow_le (ι := ι₂) (B.image (g - ·)) p
    rw [card_image_of_injective _ (sub_right_injective), hm] at h1
    calc (∑ c : ι₂ → G, (hit (B.image (g - ·)) c : ℝ) ^ p) / lam ^ p
        ≤ 2 ^ 2 ^ p * (N : ℝ) ^ m * max 1 ((2 : ℝ) ^ m * #B / N) ^ p / lam ^ p := by gcongr
      _ = 2 ^ 2 ^ p * (N : ℝ) ^ m * (max 1 ((2 : ℝ) ^ m * #B / N) / lam) ^ p := by
          rw [mul_div_assoc, ← div_pow]
      _ ≤ 2 ^ 2 ^ p * (N : ℝ) ^ m * (1 / K) ^ p := by
          gcongr
      _ = 2 ^ 2 ^ p * (N : ℝ) ^ m / K ^ p := by rw [one_div_pow]; ring
  calc (#{c : ι₂ → G | ¬ Bal ε (Sum.elim a c)} : ℝ)
      ≤ ∑ g : G, (#({c | lam ^ p ≤ (hit (B.image (g - ·)) c : ℝ) ^ p} : Finset (ι₂ → G)) : ℝ) := by
        exact_mod_cast (card_le_card hsub).trans card_biUnion_le
    _ ≤ ∑ g : G, (∑ c : ι₂ → G, (hit (B.image (g - ·)) c : ℝ) ^ p) / lam ^ p := by
        gcongr with g
        exact card_le_sum_div _ (fun c => by positivity) (by positivity)
    _ ≤ ∑ _g : G, 2 ^ 2 ^ p * (N : ℝ) ^ m / K ^ p := Finset.sum_le_sum fun g _ => hmom g
    _ = N * (2 ^ 2 ^ p * (N : ℝ) ^ m / K ^ p) := by rw [sum_const, card_univ, nsmul_eq_mul]
    _ ≤ 2 ^ 2 ^ p * (N : ℝ) ^ m / N := by
        rw [mul_div_assoc', div_le_div_iff₀ (by positivity) hN]
        calc (N : ℝ) * (2 ^ 2 ^ p * N ^ m) * N = 2 ^ 2 ^ p * N ^ m * N ^ 2 := by ring
          _ ≤ 2 ^ 2 ^ p * N ^ m * K ^ p := by gcongr

open scoped Classical in
/-- **Failure count for independent uniform tuples.** -/
private theorem card_not_bal_le_of_split (k₁ m p : ℕ) (hk₁ : Fintype.card ι₁ = k₁)
    (hm : Fintype.card ι₂ = m) {ε K t : ℝ} (hε : 0 < ε) (hε1 : ε ≤ 1) (hK : 1 ≤ K) (ht : 1 ≤ t)
    (hKp : (Fintype.card G : ℝ) ^ 2 ≤ K ^ p) (hm' : 2 * K ^ 2 ≤ 2 ^ m * ε)
    (hk' : 8 * t * K ^ 2 * Fintype.card G ≤ 2 ^ k₁ * ε ^ 3) :
    (#{f : ι₁ ⊕ ι₂ → G | ¬ Bal ε f} : ℝ) ≤
      (1 / t + 2 * 2 ^ 2 ^ p / Fintype.card G) * (Fintype.card G : ℝ) ^ (k₁ + m) := by
  set N := Fintype.card G
  set μ₁ : ℝ := 2 ^ k₁ / N with hμ₁def
  have hN : (0 : ℝ) < N := by exact_mod_cast Fintype.card_pos
  have ht0 : 0 < t := by linarith
  have hμ : (N : ℝ) ≤ 2 ^ k₁ := by
    have h1 : (N : ℝ) ≤ 8 * t * K ^ 2 * N := by
      have : (1 : ℝ) ≤ 8 * t * K ^ 2 := by nlinarith
      nlinarith
    have h2 : (2 : ℝ) ^ k₁ * ε ^ 3 ≤ 2 ^ k₁ := by
      have : ε ^ 3 ≤ 1 := pow_le_one₀ hε.le hε1
      nlinarith [pow_pos (two_pos (α := ℝ)) k₁]
    linarith
  -- good first blocks
  set Good : (ι₁ → G) → Prop := fun a => (∑ h, ((cnt a h : ℝ) - μ₁) ^ 2 ≤ t * 2 ^ k₁) ∧
    ∀ h, (cnt a h : ℝ) ≤ K * μ₁ with hGood
  have hbadA : (#{a : ι₁ → G | ¬ Good a} : ℝ) ≤ (N : ℝ) ^ k₁ / t + 2 ^ 2 ^ p * (N : ℝ) ^ k₁ / N :=
    card_not_good_le k₁ p hk₁ hK ht0 hKp hμ
  have hsplit : (#{f : ι₁ ⊕ ι₂ → G | ¬ Bal ε f} : ℝ) =
      ∑ a : ι₁ → G, (#{c : ι₂ → G | ¬ Bal ε (Sum.elim a c)} : ℝ) := by
    rw [Finset.card_equiv (Equiv.sumArrowEquivProdArrow ι₁ ι₂ G)
      (t := {x : (ι₁ → G) × (ι₂ → G) | ¬ Bal ε (Sum.elim x.1 x.2)}) (fun f => by
        simp [Equiv.sumArrowEquivProdArrow, Sum.elim_comp_inl_inr])]
    simp only [card_filter, Nat.cast_sum, Nat.cast_ite, Nat.cast_one, Nat.cast_zero]
    exact Fintype.sum_prod_type _
  have hper : ∀ a : ι₁ → G, (#{c : ι₂ → G | ¬ Bal ε (Sum.elim a c)} : ℝ) ≤
      (if Good a then 0 else (N : ℝ) ^ m) + 2 ^ 2 ^ p * (N : ℝ) ^ m / N := by
    intro a
    by_cases ha : Good a
    · rw [ite_eq_left ha, zero_add]
      exact card_not_bal_le a k₁ m p hk₁ hm hε hK ht0 hKp hm' hk' ha.1 ha.2
    · rw [ite_eq_right ha]
      have h1 : (#{c : ι₂ → G | ¬ Bal ε (Sum.elim a c)} : ℝ) ≤ (N : ℝ) ^ m := by
        have := card_le_univ ({c : ι₂ → G | ¬ Bal ε (Sum.elim a c)} : Finset _)
        rw [Fintype.card_fun, hm] at this
        exact_mod_cast this
      have : (0 : ℝ) ≤ 2 ^ 2 ^ p * (N : ℝ) ^ m / N := by positivity
      linarith
  have hcount : ∑ a : ι₁ → G, (if Good a then (0 : ℝ) else (N : ℝ) ^ m) =
      (#{a : ι₁ → G | ¬ Good a} : ℝ) * (N : ℝ) ^ m := by
    rw [Finset.sum_ite, sum_const_zero, zero_add, sum_const, nsmul_eq_mul]
  have hcardA : (Fintype.card (ι₁ → G) : ℝ) = (N : ℝ) ^ k₁ := by
    rw [Fintype.card_fun, hk₁]; push_cast; rfl
  calc (#{f : ι₁ ⊕ ι₂ → G | ¬ Bal ε f} : ℝ)
      = ∑ a : ι₁ → G, (#{c : ι₂ → G | ¬ Bal ε (Sum.elim a c)} : ℝ) := hsplit
    _ ≤ ∑ a : ι₁ → G, ((if Good a then 0 else (N : ℝ) ^ m) + 2 ^ 2 ^ p * (N : ℝ) ^ m / N) :=
        sum_le_sum fun a _ => hper a
    _ = (#{a : ι₁ → G | ¬ Good a} : ℝ) * (N : ℝ) ^ m +
          (N : ℝ) ^ k₁ * (2 ^ 2 ^ p * (N : ℝ) ^ m / N) := by
        rw [sum_add_distrib, hcount, sum_const, card_univ, nsmul_eq_mul, hcardA]
    _ ≤ ((N : ℝ) ^ k₁ / t + 2 ^ 2 ^ p * (N : ℝ) ^ k₁ / N) * (N : ℝ) ^ m +
          (N : ℝ) ^ k₁ * (2 ^ 2 ^ p * (N : ℝ) ^ m / N) := by gcongr
    _ = (1 / t + 2 * 2 ^ 2 ^ p / N) * (N : ℝ) ^ (k₁ + m) := by
        rw [pow_add]
        field_simp
        ring

end Split2

/-! ### From tuples to uniformly random subsets -/

omit [Fintype G] [DecidableEq ι] in
private lemma subsetSumCount_image {f : ι → G} (hf : Function.Injective f) (g : G) :
    subsetSumCount (univ.image f) g = cnt f g := by
  classical
  unfold subsetSumCount cnt
  symm
  refine card_bij (fun s _ => s.image f) ?_ ?_ ?_
  · intro s hs
    simp only [mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and] at hs
    simp only [mem_filter, mem_powerset]
    refine ⟨image_subset_image (subset_univ s), ?_⟩
    rw [sum_image (fun x _ y _ h => hf h)]
    exact hs
  · intro s _ s' _ h
    exact image_injective hf h
  · intro S hS
    simp only [mem_filter, mem_powerset] at hS
    have hSeq : (univ.filter (fun j => f j ∈ S)).image f = S := by
      ext x
      simp only [mem_image, mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and]
      constructor
      · rintro ⟨j, hj, rfl⟩; exact hj
      · intro hx
        obtain ⟨j, _, rfl⟩ := mem_image.1 (hS.1 hx)
        exact ⟨j, hx, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨univ.filter (fun j => f j ∈ S), ?_, hSeq⟩
    simp only [mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and]
    have := sum_image (f := fun x => x) (s := univ.filter (fun j => f j ∈ S)) (g := f)
      (fun x _ y _ h => hf h)
    rw [← this, hSeq]
    exact hS.2

omit [DecidableEq ι] in
private lemma bal_iff_isBalanced {ε : ℝ} {f : ι → G} (hf : Function.Injective f) :
    Bal ε f ↔ IsBalanced ε (univ.image f) := by
  unfold Bal IsBalanced
  rw [card_image_of_injective _ hf, card_univ]
  simp only [subsetSumCount_image hf]

omit [AddCommGroup G] in
/-- Each `k`-subset is the image of at least `k!` injective tuples. -/
private lemma factorial_le_card_image_eq {A : Finset G} (hA : #A = Fintype.card ι) :
    (Fintype.card ι).factorial ≤ #{f : ι → G | Function.Injective f ∧ univ.image f = A} := by
  have e0 : ι ≃ A := Fintype.equivOfCardEq (by rw [Fintype.card_coe, hA])
  rw [← Fintype.card_equiv e0]
  rw [← card_univ]
  refine card_le_card_of_injOn (fun e i => (e i : G)) ?_ ?_
  · intro e _
    simp only [coe_filter, mem_univ, true_and, Set.mem_ofPred_eq]
    refine ⟨fun i j h => e.injective (Subtype.ext h), ?_⟩
    ext x
    simp only [mem_image, mem_univ, true_and]
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨i, rfl⟩; exact (e i).2
    · intro hx; exact ⟨e.symm ⟨x, hx⟩, by simp⟩
  · intro e _ e' _ h
    ext i
    exact congrFun h i

open scoped Classical in
/-- **From independent tuples to uniform `k`-subsets.** -/
private lemma one_sub_balancedProbability_le (ε : ℝ) (hk : Fintype.card ι ≤ Fintype.card G) :
    1 - balancedProbability G ε (Fintype.card ι) ≤
      (#{f : ι → G | ¬ Bal ε f} : ℝ) / (Fintype.card G).descFactorial (Fintype.card ι) := by
  set k := Fintype.card ι
  set N := Fintype.card G
  set P := (univ : Finset G).powersetCard k
  have hP : #P = N.choose k := by rw [card_powersetCard, card_univ]
  have hPpos : (0 : ℝ) < #P := by
    rw [hP]; exact_mod_cast Nat.choose_pos hk
  have hdesc : (N.descFactorial k : ℝ) = k.factorial * #P := by
    rw [hP, Nat.descFactorial_eq_factorial_mul_choose]; push_cast; ring
  have hfact : (0 : ℝ) < k.factorial := by exact_mod_cast Nat.factorial_pos k
  -- `k! · #(bad k-subsets) ≤ #(bad tuples)`
  have hbad : (k.factorial : ℝ) * #(P.filter fun A => ¬ IsBalanced ε A) ≤
      #{f : ι → G | ¬ Bal ε f} := by
    have h1 : #{f : ι → G | Function.Injective f ∧
          univ.image f ∈ P.filter fun A => ¬ IsBalanced ε A}
        = ∑ A ∈ P.filter (fun A => ¬ IsBalanced ε A),
          #{f : ι → G | Function.Injective f ∧ univ.image f = A} := by
      rw [card_eq_sum_card_fiberwise (f := fun f : ι → G => univ.image f)
        (fun f hf => mem_coe.2 (mem_filter.1 (mem_coe.1 hf)).2.2)]
      refine sum_congr rfl fun A hA => ?_
      congr 1
      ext f
      simp only [mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and]
      constructor
      · rintro ⟨⟨hf, _⟩, h⟩; exact ⟨hf, h⟩
      · rintro ⟨hf, h⟩; subst h; exact ⟨⟨hf, mem_filter.1 hA⟩, rfl⟩
    have h2 : ∑ A ∈ P.filter (fun A => ¬ IsBalanced ε A),
          #{f : ι → G | Function.Injective f ∧ univ.image f = A} ≥
        ∑ _A ∈ P.filter (fun A => ¬ IsBalanced ε A), k.factorial := by
      refine sum_le_sum fun A hA => ?_
      have hA' : #A = k := (mem_powersetCard.1 (mem_filter.1 hA).1).2
      exact factorial_le_card_image_eq hA'
    have h3 : #{f : ι → G | Function.Injective f ∧
          univ.image f ∈ P.filter fun A => ¬ IsBalanced ε A}
        ≤ #{f : ι → G | ¬ Bal ε f} := by
      refine card_le_card fun f hf => ?_
      simp only [mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and] at hf ⊢
      rw [bal_iff_isBalanced hf.1]
      exact hf.2.2
    rw [sum_const, smul_eq_mul] at h2
    have := (h2.trans_eq h1.symm).trans h3
    rw [mul_comm]
    exact_mod_cast this
  have hsplit : (#(P.filter (IsBalanced ε)) : ℝ) + #(P.filter fun A => ¬ IsBalanced ε A) = #P := by
    exact_mod_cast card_filter_add_card_filter_not _
  change 1 - (#(P.filter (IsBalanced ε)) : ℝ) / #P ≤ _
  have e : 1 - (#(P.filter (IsBalanced ε)) : ℝ) / #P =
      #(P.filter fun A => ¬ IsBalanced ε A) / #P := by
    rw [eq_div_iff hPpos.ne', sub_mul, div_mul_cancel₀ _ hPpos.ne', one_mul]
    linarith
  rw [e, hdesc, div_le_div_iff₀ hPpos (by positivity)]
  nlinarith

/-- The falling factorial is at least half the power when `2 k² ≤ N`. -/
private lemma descFactorial_ge (N k : ℕ) (h : 2 * k ^ 2 ≤ N) :
    (N : ℝ) ^ k / 2 ≤ N.descFactorial k := by
  rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos k with rfl | hk0
  · norm_num
  have hN : (0 : ℝ) < N := by
    have : 0 < N := lt_of_lt_of_le (by positivity) h
    exact_mod_cast this
  have hkN : k ≤ N := by nlinarith
  have h1 : ((N - k : ℝ)) ^ k ≤ N.descFactorial k := by
    have := Nat.pow_sub_le_descFactorial N k
    have h2 : (N - k : ℝ) ≤ ((N + 1 - k : ℕ) : ℝ) := by
      rw [Nat.cast_sub (by omega)]; push_cast; linarith
    calc (N - k : ℝ) ^ k ≤ ((N + 1 - k : ℕ) : ℝ) ^ k := by
          gcongr
          have : (k : ℝ) ≤ N := by exact_mod_cast hkN
          linarith
      _ ≤ N.descFactorial k := by exact_mod_cast this
  have h3 : (N : ℝ) ^ k / 2 ≤ (N - k : ℝ) ^ k := by
    have hkN' : (k : ℝ) / N ≤ 1 := (div_le_one hN).2 (by exact_mod_cast hkN)
    have hb := one_add_mul_le_pow (a := -(k : ℝ) / N) (by rw [neg_div]; linarith) k
    have hkk : (2 : ℝ) * k ^ 2 ≤ N := by exact_mod_cast h
    have e : (N - k : ℝ) ^ k = N ^ k * (1 + -(k : ℝ) / N) ^ k := by
      rw [← mul_pow]; congr 1; field_simp; ring
    rw [e]
    have hk2 : (k : ℝ) ^ 2 / N ≤ 1 / 2 := by rw [div_le_iff₀ hN]; linarith
    have e2 : (1 : ℝ) + k * (-(k : ℝ) / N) = 1 - k ^ 2 / N := by ring
    have : (1 : ℝ) / 2 ≤ 1 + k * (-(k : ℝ) / N) := by rw [e2]; linarith
    calc (N : ℝ) ^ k / 2 = N ^ k * (1 / 2) := by ring
      _ ≤ N ^ k * (1 + k * (-(k : ℝ) / N)) := by gcongr
      _ ≤ N ^ k * (1 + -(k : ℝ) / N) ^ k := by gcongr
  linarith

/-! ### Parameters and limits -/

/-- An exponent with `8 / ε ^ 3 ≤ 2 ^ expC ε`. -/
private noncomputable def expC (ε : ℝ) : ℕ := Nat.clog 2 ⌈8 / ε ^ 3⌉₊

private lemma expC_spec (ε : ℝ) : 8 / ε ^ 3 ≤ (2 : ℝ) ^ expC ε :=
  (Nat.le_ceil _).trans (by exact_mod_cast Nat.le_pow_clog one_lt_two _)

/-- The moment order used for groups of order `N`. -/
private def momOrd (N : ℕ) : ℕ := Nat.log 2 (Nat.log 2 N) - 1

/-- The block parameter: `2 ^ blk N` is the threshold `K`. -/
private def blk (N : ℕ) : ℕ := 2 * Nat.clog 2 N / momOrd N + 1

/-- The size of the first block of random elements. -/
private noncomputable def sizeOne (ε : ℝ) (N : ℕ) : ℕ :=
  Nat.clog 2 N + 2 * blk N + expC ε + momOrd N

/-- The size of the second block of random elements. -/
private noncomputable def sizeTwo (ε : ℝ) (N : ℕ) : ℕ := 2 * blk N + expC ε + 1

/-- The subset size `k(N)`. -/
private noncomputable def subsetSize (ε : ℝ) (N : ℕ) : ℕ := sizeOne ε N + sizeTwo ε N

private lemma subsetSize_eq (ε : ℝ) (N : ℕ) :
    subsetSize ε N = Nat.clog 2 N + 4 * blk N + 2 * expC ε + momOrd N + 1 := by
  unfold subsetSize sizeOne sizeTwo; ring

/-- `2 ^ (2 ^ p) * 2 ^ p ≤ N` for the moment order `p` of `N`. -/
private lemma two_pow_two_pow_mul_le {N : ℕ} (hp : 1 ≤ momOrd N) :
    2 ^ 2 ^ momOrd N * 2 ^ momOrd N ≤ N := by
  have hℓ : 2 ≤ Nat.log 2 (Nat.log 2 N) := by unfold momOrd at hp; omega
  have hℓ0 : Nat.log 2 N ≠ 0 := by
    intro h; rw [h, Nat.log_zero_right] at hℓ; omega
  have hN0 : N ≠ 0 := by
    intro h; apply hℓ0; simp [h]
  have h1 : momOrd N + 1 = Nat.log 2 (Nat.log 2 N) := by unfold momOrd; omega
  have h2 : 2 ^ (momOrd N + 1) ≤ Nat.log 2 N := by rw [h1]; exact Nat.pow_log_le_self 2 hℓ0
  have h3 : 2 ^ Nat.log 2 N ≤ N := Nat.pow_log_le_self 2 hN0
  calc 2 ^ 2 ^ momOrd N * 2 ^ momOrd N ≤ 2 ^ 2 ^ momOrd N * 2 ^ 2 ^ momOrd N := by
        gcongr
        exact Nat.lt_two_pow_self.le
    _ = 2 ^ 2 ^ (momOrd N + 1) := by rw [← pow_add, pow_succ]; ring_nf
    _ ≤ 2 ^ Nat.log 2 N := Nat.pow_le_pow_right (by norm_num) h2
    _ ≤ N := h3

open scoped Classical in
/-- **The failure probability for groups of order `N`.** -/
private lemma one_sub_balancedProbability_le_of {ε : ℝ} (hε : 0 < ε) (hε1 : ε ≤ 1) (G : Type*)
    [AddCommGroup G] [Fintype G] (hp : 1 ≤ momOrd (Fintype.card G))
    (hk : 2 * subsetSize ε (Fintype.card G) ^ 2 ≤ Fintype.card G) :
    1 - balancedProbability G ε (subsetSize ε (Fintype.card G)) ≤
      6 / 2 ^ momOrd (Fintype.card G) := by
  classical
  set N := Fintype.card G
  set p := momOrd N
  set L := Nat.clog 2 N
  set q := blk N
  set c := expC ε
  set k₁ := sizeOne ε N
  set m := sizeTwo ε N
  have hN : (0 : ℝ) < N := by exact_mod_cast Fintype.card_pos
  have hNL : (N : ℝ) ≤ 2 ^ L := by exact_mod_cast Nat.le_pow_clog one_lt_two N
  have hc3 : 8 ≤ (2 : ℝ) ^ c * ε ^ 3 := by
    have := expC_spec ε
    rwa [div_le_iff₀ (by positivity)] at this
  have hc1 : 1 ≤ (2 : ℝ) ^ c * ε := by
    have h3 : ε ^ 3 ≤ ε := by
      have : ε ^ 2 ≤ 1 := pow_le_one₀ hε.le hε1
      nlinarith
    nlinarith [pow_pos (two_pos (α := ℝ)) c]
  have hqp : 2 * L ≤ q * p := by
    have := Nat.lt_div_mul_add (a := 2 * L) (show 0 < p by omega)
    change 2 * L ≤ (2 * L / p + 1) * p
    rw [add_mul, one_mul]; omega
  set K : ℝ := 2 ^ q with hKdef
  set t : ℝ := 2 ^ p with htdef
  have hK : 1 ≤ K := one_le_pow₀ (by norm_num)
  have ht : 1 ≤ t := one_le_pow₀ (by norm_num)
  have hKp : (N : ℝ) ^ 2 ≤ K ^ p := by
    calc (N : ℝ) ^ 2 ≤ (2 ^ L) ^ 2 := by gcongr
      _ = 2 ^ (2 * L) := by rw [← pow_mul, mul_comm]
      _ ≤ 2 ^ (q * p) := pow_le_pow_right₀ (by norm_num) hqp
      _ = K ^ p := by rw [hKdef, pow_mul]
  have hm' : 2 * K ^ 2 ≤ 2 ^ m * ε := by
    have e : (2 : ℝ) ^ m = K ^ 2 * 2 ^ c * 2 := by
      change (2 : ℝ) ^ (2 * q + c + 1) = _
      rw [pow_add, pow_add, pow_mul, hKdef, ← pow_mul, ← pow_mul, mul_comm q 2]; ring
    rw [e]
    have hK2 : 0 ≤ K ^ 2 := by positivity
    nlinarith
  have hk' : 8 * t * K ^ 2 * N ≤ 2 ^ k₁ * ε ^ 3 := by
    have e : (2 : ℝ) ^ k₁ = 2 ^ L * K ^ 2 * 2 ^ c * t := by
      change (2 : ℝ) ^ (L + 2 * q + c + p) = _
      rw [pow_add, pow_add, pow_add, hKdef, htdef, ← pow_mul, mul_comm q 2]
    rw [e]
    have hKt : 0 ≤ K ^ 2 * t := by positivity
    calc 8 * t * K ^ 2 * N = (K ^ 2 * t) * (8 * N) := by ring
      _ ≤ (K ^ 2 * t) * ((2 ^ c * ε ^ 3) * 2 ^ L) := by gcongr
      _ = 2 ^ L * K ^ 2 * 2 ^ c * t * ε ^ 3 := by ring
  have hbad := card_not_bal_le_of_split (G := G) (ι₁ := Fin k₁) (ι₂ := Fin m) k₁ m p
    (Fintype.card_fin _) (Fintype.card_fin _) hε hε1 hK ht hKp hm' hk'
  have hcard : Fintype.card (Fin k₁ ⊕ Fin m) = subsetSize ε N := by
    rw [Fintype.card_sum, Fintype.card_fin, Fintype.card_fin]; rfl
  have hkN : subsetSize ε N ≤ N := by nlinarith
  have htr := one_sub_balancedProbability_le (G := G) (ι := Fin k₁ ⊕ Fin m) ε (hcard ▸ hkN)
  rw [hcard] at htr
  have hdesc := descFactorial_ge N (subsetSize ε N) hk
  have h4 : (2 : ℝ) ^ 2 ^ p / N ≤ 1 / 2 ^ p := by
    rw [div_le_div_iff₀ hN (by positivity), one_mul]
    exact_mod_cast two_pow_two_pow_mul_le hp
  have hpos : (0 : ℝ) < (N : ℝ) ^ subsetSize ε N / 2 := by positivity
  calc 1 - balancedProbability G ε (subsetSize ε N)
      ≤ (#{f : Fin k₁ ⊕ Fin m → G | ¬ Bal ε f} : ℝ) / N.descFactorial (subsetSize ε N) := htr
    _ ≤ ((1 / t + 2 * 2 ^ 2 ^ p / N) * (N : ℝ) ^ (k₁ + m)) / ((N : ℝ) ^ subsetSize ε N / 2) := by
        gcongr
    _ = 2 * (1 / t + 2 * (2 ^ 2 ^ p / N)) := by
        have : k₁ + m = subsetSize ε N := rfl
        rw [this]
        field_simp
    _ ≤ 2 * (1 / 2 ^ p + 2 * (1 / 2 ^ p)) := by rw [htdef]; gcongr
    _ = 6 / 2 ^ p := by ring

private lemma tendsto_momOrd : Tendsto momOrd atTop atTop := by
  rw [tendsto_atTop]
  intro j
  rw [eventually_atTop]
  refine ⟨2 ^ 2 ^ (j + 1), fun N hN => ?_⟩
  have h1 : 2 ^ (j + 1) ≤ Nat.log 2 N := Nat.le_log_of_pow_le one_lt_two hN
  have h2 : j + 1 ≤ Nat.log 2 (Nat.log 2 N) := Nat.le_log_of_pow_le one_lt_two h1
  unfold momOrd
  omega

private lemma two_pow_momOrd_le_logb {N : ℕ} (hp : 1 ≤ momOrd N) :
    (2 : ℝ) ^ momOrd N ≤ Real.logb 2 N := by
  have hℓ : 2 ≤ Nat.log 2 (Nat.log 2 N) := by unfold momOrd at hp; omega
  have hℓ0 : Nat.log 2 N ≠ 0 := by
    intro h; rw [h, Nat.log_zero_right] at hℓ; omega
  have h1 : momOrd N + 1 = Nat.log 2 (Nat.log 2 N) := by unfold momOrd; omega
  have h2 : 2 ^ (momOrd N + 1) ≤ Nat.log 2 N := by rw [h1]; exact Nat.pow_log_le_self 2 hℓ0
  have h3 : 2 ^ momOrd N ≤ Nat.log 2 N :=
    (Nat.pow_le_pow_right (by norm_num) (Nat.le_succ _)).trans h2
  calc (2 : ℝ) ^ momOrd N ≤ (Nat.log 2 N : ℝ) := by exact_mod_cast h3
    _ ≤ Real.logb 2 N := by exact_mod_cast Real.natLog_le_logb N 2

private lemma logb_le_clog {N : ℕ} (hN : 1 ≤ N) : Real.logb 2 N ≤ Nat.clog 2 N := by
  have h := Nat.le_pow_clog one_lt_two N
  calc Real.logb 2 N ≤ Real.logb 2 ((2 : ℝ) ^ Nat.clog 2 N) :=
        Real.logb_le_logb_of_le one_lt_two (by exact_mod_cast hN) (by exact_mod_cast h)
    _ = Nat.clog 2 N := by rw [Real.logb_pow, Real.logb_self_eq_one one_lt_two, mul_one]

private lemma clog_le_logb_add_one {N : ℕ} (hN : 2 ≤ N) :
    (Nat.clog 2 N : ℝ) ≤ Real.logb 2 N + 1 := by
  have h := Nat.pow_pred_clog_lt_self 2 (show 1 < N by omega)
  have hpos := Nat.clog_pos one_lt_two (show 1 < N by omega)
  have h1 : ((Nat.clog 2 N).pred : ℝ) ≤ Real.logb 2 N := by
    calc ((Nat.clog 2 N).pred : ℝ) = Real.logb 2 ((2 : ℝ) ^ (Nat.clog 2 N).pred) := by
          rw [Real.logb_pow, Real.logb_self_eq_one one_lt_two, mul_one]
      _ ≤ Real.logb 2 N :=
          Real.logb_le_logb_of_le one_lt_two (by positivity) (by exact_mod_cast h.le)
  have e : ((Nat.clog 2 N).pred : ℝ) = Nat.clog 2 N - 1 := by
    rw [Nat.pred_eq_sub_one, Nat.cast_sub hpos]; simp
  linarith

private lemma subsetSize_le (ε : ℝ) {N : ℕ} (hN : 2 ≤ N) (hp : 1 ≤ momOrd N) :
    (subsetSize ε N : ℝ) ≤
      (Real.logb 2 N + 1) * (1 + 8 / momOrd N) + (2 * expC ε + 5) + momOrd N := by
  rw [subsetSize_eq]
  push_cast
  have hp0 : (0 : ℝ) < momOrd N := by exact_mod_cast hp
  have hq : (blk N : ℝ) ≤ 2 * Nat.clog 2 N / momOrd N + 1 := by
    unfold blk
    push_cast
    have := Nat.cast_div_le (α := ℝ) (m := 2 * Nat.clog 2 N) (n := momOrd N)
    push_cast at this
    linarith
  have hL := clog_le_logb_add_one hN
  have h8 : (0 : ℝ) ≤ 1 + 8 / momOrd N := by positivity
  calc (Nat.clog 2 N : ℝ) + 4 * blk N + 2 * expC ε + momOrd N + 1
      ≤ Nat.clog 2 N + 4 * (2 * Nat.clog 2 N / momOrd N + 1) + 2 * expC ε + momOrd N + 1 := by
        gcongr
    _ = Nat.clog 2 N * (1 + 8 / momOrd N) + (2 * expC ε + 5) + momOrd N := by
        field_simp
        ring
    _ ≤ (Real.logb 2 N + 1) * (1 + 8 / momOrd N) + (2 * expC ε + 5) + momOrd N := by gcongr

/-- **The subset size is asymptotic to `log₂ N`.** -/
private lemma tendsto_subsetSize_div_logb (ε : ℝ) :
    Tendsto (fun N : ℕ => (subsetSize ε N : ℝ) / Real.logb 2 N) atTop (nhds 1) := by
  have hX : Tendsto (fun N : ℕ => Real.logb 2 N) atTop atTop :=
    (Real.tendsto_logb_atTop one_lt_two).comp tendsto_natCast_atTop_atTop
  have hp : Tendsto (fun N : ℕ => (momOrd N : ℝ)) atTop atTop :=
    tendsto_natCast_atTop_atTop.comp tendsto_momOrd
  set u : ℕ → ℝ := fun N => (1 + 1 / Real.logb 2 N) * (1 + 8 / momOrd N) +
    (2 * expC ε + 5) / Real.logb 2 N + momOrd N / 2 ^ momOrd N with hudef
  have hu : Tendsto u atTop (nhds 1) := by
    have h1 : Tendsto (fun N : ℕ => 1 / Real.logb 2 N) atTop (nhds 0) :=
      tendsto_const_nhds.div_atTop hX
    have h2 : Tendsto (fun N : ℕ => 8 / (momOrd N : ℝ)) atTop (nhds 0) :=
      tendsto_const_nhds.div_atTop hp
    have h3 : Tendsto (fun N : ℕ => (2 * expC ε + 5 : ℝ) / Real.logb 2 N) atTop (nhds 0) :=
      tendsto_const_nhds.div_atTop hX
    have h4 : Tendsto (fun N : ℕ => (momOrd N : ℝ) / 2 ^ momOrd N) atTop (nhds 0) := by
      have := (tendsto_pow_const_div_const_pow_of_one_lt 1 (one_lt_two (α := ℝ))).comp
        tendsto_momOrd
      simp only [pow_one] at this
      exact this
    have := ((((tendsto_const_nhds (x := (1 : ℝ))).add h1).mul
      ((tendsto_const_nhds (x := (1 : ℝ))).add h2)).add h3).add h4
    simpa [hudef] using this
  refine tendsto_of_tendsto_of_tendsto_of_le_of_le' tendsto_const_nhds hu ?_ ?_
  · filter_upwards [eventually_ge_atTop 2] with N hN
    have hXpos : 0 < Real.logb 2 N := Real.logb_pos one_lt_two (by exact_mod_cast hN)
    rw [le_div_iff₀ hXpos, one_mul]
    calc Real.logb 2 N ≤ Nat.clog 2 N := logb_le_clog (by omega)
      _ ≤ subsetSize ε N := by
          rw [subsetSize_eq]; push_cast
          have : (0 : ℝ) ≤ 4 * blk N + 2 * expC ε + momOrd N + 1 := by positivity
          linarith
  · filter_upwards [eventually_ge_atTop 2, tendsto_momOrd.eventually_ge_atTop 1] with N hN hp1
    have hXpos : 0 < Real.logb 2 N := Real.logb_pos one_lt_two (by exact_mod_cast hN)
    have hS := subsetSize_le ε hN hp1
    have h2p := two_pow_momOrd_le_logb hp1
    have hp0 : (0 : ℝ) < momOrd N := by exact_mod_cast hp1
    rw [div_le_iff₀ hXpos, hudef]
    have hpX : (momOrd N : ℝ) ≤ momOrd N / 2 ^ momOrd N * Real.logb 2 N := by
      rw [div_mul_eq_mul_div, le_div_iff₀ (by positivity)]
      gcongr
    have e : ((1 + 1 / Real.logb 2 N) * (1 + 8 / momOrd N) + (2 * expC ε + 5) / Real.logb 2 N +
        momOrd N / 2 ^ momOrd N) * Real.logb 2 N =
        (Real.logb 2 N + 1) * (1 + 8 / momOrd N) + (2 * expC ε + 5) +
          momOrd N / 2 ^ momOrd N * Real.logb 2 N := by
      field_simp
    rw [e]
    linarith

/-- **Eventually `2 k(N) ^ 2 ≤ N`.** -/
private lemma eventually_two_mul_subsetSize_sq_le (ε : ℝ) :
    ∀ᶠ N : ℕ in atTop, 2 * subsetSize ε N ^ 2 ≤ N := by
  set C : ℝ := 2 * expC ε + 14 with hC
  have hlim : Tendsto (fun N : ℕ => 2 * (10 * Real.logb 2 N + C) ^ 2 / N) atTop (nhds 0) := by
    have hA := Real.tendsto_pow_logb_div_mul_add_atTop (b := 2) 1 0 2 one_ne_zero
    have hB := Real.tendsto_pow_logb_div_mul_add_atTop (b := 2) 1 0 1 one_ne_zero
    have hD : Tendsto (fun x : ℝ => 1 / x) atTop (nhds 0) := tendsto_const_nhds.div_atTop tendsto_id
    have := (((hA.const_mul 200).add (hB.const_mul (40 * C))).add (hD.const_mul (2 * C ^ 2))).comp
      tendsto_natCast_atTop_atTop
    simp only [mul_zero, add_zero] at this
    refine this.congr fun N => ?_
    simp only [Function.comp, one_mul, pow_one]
    ring
  filter_upwards [hlim.eventually (gt_mem_nhds one_pos), eventually_ge_atTop 2,
    tendsto_momOrd.eventually_ge_atTop 1] with N h1 hN hp
  have hNpos : (0 : ℝ) < N := by exact_mod_cast (show 0 < N by omega)
  have hS := subsetSize_le ε hN hp
  have h2p := two_pow_momOrd_le_logb hp
  have hXpos : 0 < Real.logb 2 N := Real.logb_pos one_lt_two (by exact_mod_cast hN)
  have hp0 : (1 : ℝ) ≤ momOrd N := by exact_mod_cast hp
  have hpX : (momOrd N : ℝ) ≤ Real.logb 2 N := by
    have : (momOrd N : ℝ) ≤ 2 ^ momOrd N := by exact_mod_cast Nat.lt_two_pow_self.le
    linarith
  have h8 : 8 / (momOrd N : ℝ) ≤ 8 := by
    rw [div_le_iff₀ (by linarith)]; nlinarith
  have hS' : (subsetSize ε N : ℝ) ≤ 10 * Real.logb 2 N + C := by
    have : (Real.logb 2 N + 1) * (1 + 8 / momOrd N) ≤ (Real.logb 2 N + 1) * 9 := by
      gcongr; linarith
    rw [hC]; linarith
  rw [div_lt_one hNpos] at h1
  have : (2 * subsetSize ε N ^ 2 : ℝ) < N := by
    calc (2 * subsetSize ε N ^ 2 : ℝ) ≤ 2 * (10 * Real.logb 2 N + C) ^ 2 := by
          gcongr
      _ < N := h1
  exact_mod_cast this.le

omit [DecidableEq G] in
private lemma sum_subsetSumCount (A : Finset G) : ∑ g, subsetSumCount A g = 2 ^ A.card := by
  classical
  rw [← card_powerset]
  rw [card_eq_sum_card_fiberwise (f := fun S : Finset G => ∑ x ∈ S, x) (t := univ)
    (fun _ _ => mem_coe.2 (mem_univ _))]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun g _ => ?_
  unfold subsetSumCount
  congr 1

omit [DecidableEq G] in
/-- **Lower bound.** An `ε`-balanced set with `ε < 1` has at least `log₂ |G|` elements. -/
private lemma card_le_two_pow_of_isBalanced {ε : ℝ} (hε1 : ε < 1) {A : Finset G}
    (hA : IsBalanced ε A) : Fintype.card G ≤ 2 ^ A.card := by
  classical
  have hpos : ∀ g, 1 ≤ subsetSumCount A g := by
    intro g
    have h := (abs_le.1 (hA g)).1
    have hμ : (0 : ℝ) < 2 ^ A.card / Fintype.card G := by
      have : (0 : ℝ) < Fintype.card G := by exact_mod_cast Fintype.card_pos
      positivity
    have : (0 : ℝ) < subsetSumCount A g := by nlinarith
    exact_mod_cast this
  calc Fintype.card G = ∑ _g : G, 1 := by simp
    _ ≤ ∑ g, subsetSumCount A g := sum_le_sum fun g _ => hpos g
    _ = 2 ^ A.card := sum_subsetSumCount A

omit [DecidableEq G] in
private lemma balancedProbability_le_one (ε : ℝ) (k : ℕ) : balancedProbability G ε k ≤ 1 := by
  classical
  unfold balancedProbability
  exact div_le_one_of_le₀ (by exact_mod_cast card_le_card (filter_subset _ _)) (by positivity)

/-! ### The main theorem -/

/--
**Erdős Problem 1179 holds.** For every real $\varepsilon$ with $0 < \varepsilon < 1$, the
following two bounds hold. Upper bound: there is a function $k : \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{N}$ with
$k(N) / \log_2 N \to 1$ as $N \to \infty$ such that, for every sequence $(G_i)_{i \in \mathbb{N}}$
of finite abelian groups with $|G_i| \to \infty$, the probability that a uniformly random
$k(|G_i|)$-element subset of $G_i$ is $\varepsilon$-balanced tends to $1$ as $i \to \infty$. Lower
bound: for every finite abelian group $G$, every $\varepsilon$-balanced subset $A \subseteq G$
satisfies $|G| \le 2^{|A|}$.

Writing $g_\varepsilon(N)$ for the least size for which a uniformly random subset of a group of
order $N$ is $\varepsilon$-balanced with probability tending to $1$, Erdős and Hall proved
$g_\varepsilon(N) \le (1 + O_\varepsilon(\log \log \log N / \log \log N)) \log_2 N$, improving the
bound $(2 + o(1)) \log_2 N + O_\varepsilon(1)$ of Erdős and Rényi; the lower bound holds because
an $\varepsilon$-balanced set with $\varepsilon < 1$ has every element of $G$ as a subset sum.
erdosproblems.com/1179 lists the problem as proved.

Source: T. F. Bloom, Erdős Problems, Problem #1179, https://www.erdosproblems.com/1179 (status
PROVED); resolution: P. Erdős and R. R. Hall,
Probabilistic methods in group theory. II, Houston J. Math. 2 (1976), 173-180,
erdosproblems.com/1179: g_ε(N) ≤ (1 + O_ε(log log log N / log log N)) log₂ N for all 0 < ε < 1.
-/
theorem balancedSubsetSumsThresholdLogTwo_holds : balancedSubsetSumsThresholdLogTwo := by
  intro ε hε hε1
  refine ⟨⟨subsetSize ε, tendsto_subsetSize_div_logb ε, ?_⟩, ?_⟩
  · intro G _ _ hG
    have hlow : Tendsto (fun i => 1 - 6 / 2 ^ momOrd (Fintype.card (G i)) : ℕ → ℝ) atTop
        (nhds 1) := by
      have h := (tendsto_const_nhds (x := (6 : ℝ))).div_atTop
        (tendsto_pow_atTop_atTop_of_one_lt (one_lt_two (α := ℝ)))
      have := (tendsto_const_nhds (x := (1 : ℝ))).sub (h.comp (tendsto_momOrd.comp hG))
      simpa using this
    refine tendsto_of_tendsto_of_tendsto_of_le_of_le' hlow tendsto_const_nhds ?_ ?_
    · have hev := (eventually_two_mul_subsetSize_sq_le ε).and
        (tendsto_momOrd.eventually_ge_atTop 1)
      filter_upwards [hG.eventually hev] with i hi
      have := one_sub_balancedProbability_le_of hε hε1.le (G i) hi.2 hi.1
      linarith
    · exact Eventually.of_forall fun i => balancedProbability_le_one ε _
  · intro G _ _ A hA
    exact card_le_two_pow_of_isBalanced hε1 hA

end MathlibExt.Combinatorics.RandomSubsetSumsBalancedErdosProblem1179Wanted
